    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d655">

                <pb facs="0831" n="719" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg719"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/1957</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Fletcher</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-14T14:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 14, 1918, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1070. My mail despatch 890, April 3 last. Minister for Foreign Affairs informs me
                    that President has referred certain features of petroleum law to a commission
                    composed of himself, Pani, Berlanga, <pb facs="0832" n="720" xml:id="pg720"/>
                    and Nieto for study and revision. It is evident that our protest has had a
                    deterrent effect.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
